          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-205ea-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-205ea-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aa36fd2771ebc3b88ec801fc55af506ae90762c47dce500f9be0f4fce1060e4f",
      "skos:note": "Goods must be returned within 30 days of seizure notice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-1-sec-205ea-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "205EA(1) Treatment of goods seized if a claim for return is made—",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) goods are seized under a seizure warrant or under\nsubsection 203B(2) or (2A), 203CA(3) or 203CB(2); and\n\n(b) the goods are seized on belief or suspicion that they are a\nprohibited psychoactive substance; and\n\n(c) a claim for the return of the goods may be made under\nsection 205B; and\n\n(d) not later than 30 days after the day the seizure notice was\nserved, a claim is made under section 205B for return of the\ngoods."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-205ea-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-205ea-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-205ea-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must return goods",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Goods seized under certain conditions.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Goods must be returned within 30 days."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-205ea-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "205EA(2) Treatment of goods seized if a claim for return is made—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-1-sec-205ea-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The authorised person who seized the goods must, subject to any\nlaw of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory permitting their\nretention, destruction or disposal, return the goods unless:\n\n(a) the goods have been dealt with under section 206; or\n\n(b) not later than 30 days after the day the claim is made, the\nCEO gives the claimant a written notice stating that the\ngoods will be condemned as forfeited if the claimant does\nnot, within 30 days after receiving the notice, institute\nproceedings against the Commonwealth:\n\n(i) to recover the goods; or\n\n(ii) for a declaration that the goods are not forfeited.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The authorised person who seized the goods must, subject to any\nlaw of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory permitting their\nretention, destruction or disposal, return the goods unless:\n\n(a) the goods have been dealt with under section 206; or\n\n(b) not later than 30 days after the day the claim is made, the\nCEO gives the claimant a written notice stating that the\ngoods will be condemned as forfeited if the claimant does\nnot, within 30 days after receiving the notice, institute\nproceedings against the Commonwealth:\n\n(i) to recover the goods; or\n\n(ii) for a declaration that the goods are not forfeited.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-205ea"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
