      "cml:premiseText": "Section 205EA(6)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The goods must be returned within a reasonable time frame after they were seized"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-205eb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "205EB Extending the period for instituting proceedings for recovery",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-1-sec-205eb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "of suspected prohibited psychoactive substances\n\n(1) A person who has been given a notice under\nparagraph 205EA(2)(b) in relation to goods may, before the end of\nthe applicable period under paragraph 205EA(4)(a), apply to a\nmagistrate for an extension, or a further extension, of the period.\n\n(2) If the magistrate is satisfied that:\n\n(a) it is necessary that the retention of the goods continue while\ninformation is assembled relating to whether the goods are a\nprohibited psychoactive substance; and\n\n(b) there has been no avoidable delay in assembling that\ninformation;\nthe magistrate may order that the period be extended, or further\nextended, for a period specified in the order.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nPsychoactive substances  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 12, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015",
      "skos:definition": "of suspected prohibited psychoactive substances\n\n(1) A person who has been given a notice under\nparagraph 205EA(2)(b) in relation to goods may, before the end of\nthe applicable period under paragraph 205EA(4)(a), apply to a\nmagistrate for an extension, or a further extension, of the period.\n\n(2) If the magistrate is satisfied that:\n\n(a) it is necessary that the retention of the goods continue while\ninformation is assembled relating to whether the goods are a\nprohibited psychoactive substance; and\n\n(b) there has been no avoidable delay in assembling that\ninformation;\nthe magistrate may order that the period be extended, or further\nextended, for a period specified in the order.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nPsychoactive substances  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 12, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-205eb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-205eb-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3a400e6c14d5c16dff16a73e55f43d5b578e4229a736cb166fc84e87f2643fc6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-1-sec-205eb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "205EB Extending the period for instituting proceedings for recovery",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "of suspected prohibited psychoactive substances\n\n(1) A person who has been given a notice under\nparagraph 205EA(2)(b) in relation to goods may, before the end of\nthe applicable period under paragraph 205EA(4)(a), apply to a\nmagistrate for an extension, or a further extension, of the period.\n\n(2) If the magistrate is satisfied that:\n\n(a) it is necessary that the retention of the goods continue while\ninformation is assembled relating to whether the goods are a\nprohibited psychoactive substance; and\n\n(b) there has been no avoidable delay in assembling that\ninformation;\nthe magistrate may order that the period be extended, or further\nextended, for a period specified in the order.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nPsychoactive substances  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 12, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015"
    },
    {
