    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-16",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16 At the end of section 360.4 of the Criminal Code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-2-sec-16"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), this Division is not intended to\nexclude or limit the concurrent operation of a law of a State or\nTerritory that makes:\n\n(a) an act or omission that is an offence against this Division; or\n\n(b) a similar act or omission;\nan offence against the law of the State or Territory.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nFirearms trafficking offences  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 12, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\n(3) Subsection (2) applies even if the law of the State or Territory does\nany one or more of the following:\n\n(a) provides for a penalty for the offence that differs from the\npenalty provided for in this Division;\n\n(b) provides for a fault element in relation to the offence that\ndiffers from the fault elements applicable to the offence\nagainst this Division;\n\n(c) provides for a defence in relation to the offence that differs\nfrom the defences applicable to the offence against this\nDivision.\n\n(4) A person punished for an offence against a law of a State or\nTerritory referred to in subsection (2) in respect of particular\nconduct cannot be punished for an offence against this Division in\nrespect of that conduct.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), this Division is not intended to\nexclude or limit the concurrent operation of a law of a State or\nTerritory that makes:\n\n(a) an act or omission that is an offence against this Division; or\n\n(b) a similar act or omission;\nan offence against the law of the State or Territory.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nFirearms trafficking offences  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 12, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\n(3) Subsection (2) applies even if the law of the State or Territory does\nany one or more of the following:\n\n(a) provides for a penalty for the offence that differs from the\npenalty provided for in this Division;\n\n(b) provides for a fault element in relation to the offence that\ndiffers from the fault elements applicable to the offence\nagainst this Division;\n\n(c) provides for a defence in relation to the offence that differs\nfrom the defences applicable to the offence against this\nDivision.\n\n(4) A person punished for an offence against a law of a State or\nTerritory referred to in subsection (2) in respect of particular\nconduct cannot be punished for an offence against this Division in\nrespect of that conduct.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-16-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-16-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-16-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f552a1e79bdc74d313b3f0f000e309faa363c9b81f8db6b9d0fb2b41f0dcea48"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-2-sec-16",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16 At the end of section 360.4 of the Criminal Code",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), this Division is not intended to\nexclude or limit the concurrent operation of a law of a State or\nTerritory that makes:\n\n(a) an act or omission that is an offence against this Division; or\n\n(b) a similar act or omission;\nan offence against the law of the State or Territory.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nFirearms trafficking offences  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 12, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\n(3) Subsection (2) applies even if the law of the State or Territory does\nany one or more of the following:\n\n(a) provides for a penalty for the offence that differs from the\npenalty provided for in this Division;\n\n(b) provides for a fault element in relation to the offence that\ndiffers from the fault elements applicable to the offence\nagainst this Division;\n\n(c) provides for a defence in relation to the offence that differs\nfrom the defences applicable to the offence against this\nDivision.\n\n(4) A person punished for an offence against a law of a State or\nTerritory referred to in subsection (2) in respect of particular\nconduct cannot be punished for an offence against this Division in\nrespect of that conduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-16-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16(2) At the end of section 360.4 of the Criminal Code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
