      "cml:logicSummary": "Definition of preparing a thing for transfer includes packaging and separating into discrete units",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "For the purposes of paragraph (d), preparing a thing for transfer includes packaging the thing or separating the thing into discrete units."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-361-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Definition of intention to transfer",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "with the intention of transferring any of it or believing that another person intends to transfer any of it;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-361-logic-descriptionlogic-6",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "ClassInclusion",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Definition of traffic in a thing that is a firearm or a firearm part includes guarding and concealing the thing",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(f) guard or conceal the thing with the intention of transferring any of it or the intention of assisting another person to transfer any of it;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-361-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "361 2  Trafficking prohibited firearms or firearm parts into",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-2-sec-361-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "Australia\nCustoms Act prohibits imports absolutely\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person imports a thing; and\n\n(b) the thing is a firearm or firearm part; and\n\n(c) the person imports the firearm or part with the intention of\ntrafficking in the firearm or part; and\n\n(d) importing the firearm or part was prohibited under the\nCustoms Act 1901 absolutely.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years or a fine of 2,500 penalty\nunits, or both.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to paragraph (1)(d).\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2.\nCustoms Act prohibits imports if requirements not met\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nFirearms trafficking offences  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 12, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\n(a) the person imports a thing; and\n\n(b) the thing is a firearm or firearm part; and\n\n(c) the person imports the firearm or part with the intention of\ntrafficking in the firearm or part; and\n\n(d) importing the firearm or part was prohibited under the\nCustoms Act 1901 unless certain requirements were met; and\n\n(e) the person fails to meet any of those requirements.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years or a fine of 2,500 penalty\nunits, or both.\n\n(4) Absolute liability applies to paragraph (3)(d).\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2.\n\n(5) Strict liability applies to paragraph (3)(e).\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1.",
      "skos:definition": "Australia\nCustoms Act prohibits imports absolutely\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person imports a thing; and\n\n(b) the thing is a firearm or firearm part; and\n\n(c) the person imports the firearm or part with the intention of\ntrafficking in the firearm or part; and\n\n(d) importing the firearm or part was prohibited under the\nCustoms Act 1901 absolutely.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years or a fine of 2,500 penalty\nunits, or both.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to paragraph (1)(d).\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2.\nCustoms Act prohibits imports if requirements not met\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nFirearms trafficking offences  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 12, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\n(a) the person imports a thing; and\n\n(b) the thing is a firearm or firearm part; and\n\n(c) the person imports the firearm or part with the intention of\ntrafficking in the firearm or part; and\n\n(d) importing the firearm or part was prohibited under the\nCustoms Act 1901 unless certain requirements were met; and\n\n(e) the person fails to meet any of those requirements.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years or a fine of 2,500 penalty\nunits, or both.\n\n(4) Absolute liability applies to paragraph (3)(d).\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2.\n\n(5) Strict liability applies to paragraph (3)(e).\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
