    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-361-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "361 4  Defence—reasonable belief that conduct is justified or excused",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-2-sec-361-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "by or under a law\n\nA person is not criminally responsible for an offence against this\nDivision if:\n\n(a) at the time of the conduct constituting the offence, the person\nwas under a mistaken but reasonable belief that the conduct\nwas justified or excused by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth or of a State or Territory; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nFirearms trafficking offences  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 12, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\n(b) had the conduct been so justified or excused—the conduct\nwould not have constituted the offence.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nparagraph (a) (see subsection 13.3(3)).",
      "skos:definition": "by or under a law\n\nA person is not criminally responsible for an offence against this\nDivision if:\n\n(a) at the time of the conduct constituting the offence, the person\nwas under a mistaken but reasonable belief that the conduct\nwas justified or excused by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth or of a State or Territory; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nFirearms trafficking offences  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 12, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\n(b) had the conduct been so justified or excused—the conduct\nwould not have constituted the offence.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nparagraph (a) (see subsection 13.3(3)).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-361-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-361-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-361-4-logic-epistemic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-361-4-logic-ltl-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3023817330ed1e46393424e00330ff09935d9b0a9cea0770f173665c92306d3f",
      "skos:note": "Defence—reasonable belief that conduct is justified or excused"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-2-sec-361-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "361 4  Defence—reasonable belief that conduct is justified or excused",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "by or under a law\n\nA person is not criminally responsible for an offence against this\nDivision if:\n\n(a) at the time of the conduct constituting the offence, the person\nwas under a mistaken but reasonable belief that the conduct\nwas justified or excused by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth or of a State or Territory; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nFirearms trafficking offences  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 12, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\n(b) had the conduct been so justified or excused—the conduct\nwould not have constituted the offence.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nparagraph (a) (see subsection 13.3(3))."
    },
