    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-3-sec-28-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "28 Transfer country’s consent to transfer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-3-sec-28-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.37",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General must, as soon as possible after the matters\nmentioned in subsection (2) are satisfied for a transfer, notify the\ntransfer country of this and ask it:\n\n(a) whether it consents to the transfer on the terms proposed in\nthe notice; and\n\n(b) to advise whether the prisoner, or the prisoner’s\nrepresentative, consents to the transfer on those terms.\n\n(2) The matters are as follows:\n\n(a) paragraphs 10(a), (e) and (f);\n\n(b) consent in writing, by any applicable State Ministers and\nTerritory Ministers, has been given to transfer on those terms.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Attorney-General must, as soon as possible after the matters\nmentioned in subsection (2) are satisfied for a transfer, notify the\ntransfer country of this and ask it:\n\n(a) whether it consents to the transfer on the terms proposed in\nthe notice; and\n\n(b) to advise whether the prisoner, or the prisoner’s\nrepresentative, consents to the transfer on those terms.\n\n(2) The matters are as follows:\n\n(a) paragraphs 10(a), (e) and (f);\n\n(b) consent in writing, by any applicable State Ministers and\nTerritory Ministers, has been given to transfer on those terms.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-3-sec-28-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-3-sec-28-2-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eb8f90a40fbba3250b684446fcf35c7e2b46b63f3b4cceff9ad9ea439441b435"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-3-sec-28-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28 Transfer country’s consent to transfer",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 37,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General must, as soon as possible after the matters\nmentioned in subsection (2) are satisfied for a transfer, notify the\ntransfer country of this and ask it:\n\n(a) whether it consents to the transfer on the terms proposed in\nthe notice; and\n\n(b) to advise whether the prisoner, or the prisoner’s\nrepresentative, consents to the transfer on those terms.\n\n(2) The matters are as follows:\n\n(a) paragraphs 10(a), (e) and (f);\n\n(b) consent in writing, by any applicable State Ministers and\nTerritory Ministers, has been given to transfer on those terms."
    },
