    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-4-sec-270-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "270 3B  Prosecutions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-4-sec-270-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.40",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Proceedings for an offence against section 270.3, where the\nconduct constituting the alleged offence occurs wholly outside\nAustralia, must not take place except with the consent in writing of\nthe Attorney-General.\n\n(2) Even though a consent in accordance with subsection (1) has not\nbeen given in relation to an offence against section 270.3:\n\n(a) a person may be arrested for the offence, and a warrant for\nthe arrest of a person for the offence may be issued and\nexecuted; and\n\n(b) a person may be charged with the offence; and\n\n(c) a person so charged may be remanded in custody or on bail;\nbut no further step in proceedings referred to in subsection (1) is to\nbe taken until such a consent has been given.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not prevent the discharge of the accused if\nproceedings are not continued within a reasonable time.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Proceedings for an offence against section 270.3, where the\nconduct constituting the alleged offence occurs wholly outside\nAustralia, must not take place except with the consent in writing of\nthe Attorney-General.\n\n(2) Even though a consent in accordance with subsection (1) has not\nbeen given in relation to an offence against section 270.3:\n\n(a) a person may be arrested for the offence, and a warrant for\nthe arrest of a person for the offence may be issued and\nexecuted; and\n\n(b) a person may be charged with the offence; and\n\n(c) a person so charged may be remanded in custody or on bail;\nbut no further step in proceedings referred to in subsection (1) is to\nbe taken until such a consent has been given.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not prevent the discharge of the accused if\nproceedings are not continued within a reasonable time.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-4-sec-270-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-4-sec-270-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-4-sec-270-2-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2d70069d30e1314c8ae2b7105e870592a63cf8159428c1254aec2003a14bd103"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-4-sec-270-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "270 3B  Prosecutions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 40,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Proceedings for an offence against section 270.3, where the\nconduct constituting the alleged offence occurs wholly outside\nAustralia, must not take place except with the consent in writing of\nthe Attorney-General.\n\n(2) Even though a consent in accordance with subsection (1) has not\nbeen given in relation to an offence against section 270.3:\n\n(a) a person may be arrested for the offence, and a warrant for\nthe arrest of a person for the offence may be issued and\nexecuted; and\n\n(b) a person may be charged with the offence; and\n\n(c) a person so charged may be remanded in custody or on bail;\nbut no further step in proceedings referred to in subsection (1) is to\nbe taken until such a consent has been given.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not prevent the discharge of the accused if\nproceedings are not continued within a reasonable time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-4-sec-270-2-ss-1",
