    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-5-sec-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 Validating airport investigations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-5-sec-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThis item applies:\n\n(a) in relation to a thing done during the relevant period in\nrelation to an investigation by a member of the Australian\nFederal Police, or a special member, in or in relation to a\nCommonwealth place; and\n\n(b) to the extent that the doing of the thing would, apart from this\nitem, be invalid or ineffective because the Commonwealth\nplace was not a designated State airport;\nif, on the day after the relevant period, the Commonwealth place was a\ndesignated State airport.\n(2)\nThe thing done is as valid and effective, and is taken always to have\nbeen as valid and effective, as it would have been had the\nCommonwealth place been a designated State airport for the purposes\nof the Commonwealth Places (Application of Laws) Act 1970 during the\nrelevant period.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nSchedule 5  Validating airport investigations\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 12, 2015\n\nNote:\nThis means relevant Crimes Act provisions validly apply in relation to the thing done\n(see subsection 5(3A) of the Commonwealth Places (Application of Laws) Act 1970).\n(3)\nHowever, this item does not affect rights or liabilities arising between\nparties to proceedings heard and finally determined by a court on or\nbefore the commencement of this Schedule, to the extent that those\nrights or liabilities arose from, or were affected by, a thing done as\ndescribed in subitem (1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThis item applies:\n\n(a) in relation to a thing done during the relevant period in\nrelation to an investigation by a member of the Australian\nFederal Police, or a special member, in or in relation to a\nCommonwealth place; and\n\n(b) to the extent that the doing of the thing would, apart from this\nitem, be invalid or ineffective because the Commonwealth\nplace was not a designated State airport;\nif, on the day after the relevant period, the Commonwealth place was a\ndesignated State airport.\n(2)\nThe thing done is as valid and effective, and is taken always to have\nbeen as valid and effective, as it would have been had the\nCommonwealth place been a designated State airport for the purposes\nof the Commonwealth Places (Application of Laws) Act 1970 during the\nrelevant period.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nSchedule 5  Validating airport investigations\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 12, 2015\n\nNote:\nThis means relevant Crimes Act provisions validly apply in relation to the thing done\n(see subsection 5(3A) of the Commonwealth Places (Application of Laws) Act 1970).\n(3)\nHowever, this item does not affect rights or liabilities arising between\nparties to proceedings heard and finally determined by a court on or\nbefore the commencement of this Schedule, to the extent that those\nrights or liabilities arose from, or were affected by, a thing done as\ndescribed in subitem (1).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-5-sec-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-5-sec-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-5-sec-2-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "85e3f3458a8e5ab6fa5c7b6c500b6af7b7a96d1c10c75ed3396f79a116309cd7",
      "skos:note": "Validating airport investigations"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-5-sec-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 Validating airport investigations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 41,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThis item applies:\n\n(a) in relation to a thing done during the relevant period in\nrelation to an investigation by a member of the Australian\nFederal Police, or a special member, in or in relation to a\nCommonwealth place; and\n\n(b) to the extent that the doing of the thing would, apart from this\nitem, be invalid or ineffective because the Commonwealth\nplace was not a designated State airport;\nif, on the day after the relevant period, the Commonwealth place was a\ndesignated State airport.\n(2)\nThe thing done is as valid and effective, and is taken always to have\nbeen as valid and effective, as it would have been had the\nCommonwealth place been a designated State airport for the purposes\nof the Commonwealth Places (Application of Laws) Act 1970 during the\nrelevant period.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nSchedule 5  Validating airport investigations\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 12, 2015\n\nNote:\nThis means relevant Crimes Act provisions validly apply in relation to the thing done\n(see subsection 5(3A) of the Commonwealth Places (Application of Laws) Act 1970).\n(3)\nHowever, this item does not affect rights or liabilities arising between\nparties to proceedings heard and finally determined by a court on or\nbefore the commencement of this Schedule, to the extent that those\nrights or liabilities arose from, or were affected by, a thing done as\ndescribed in subitem (1)."
    },
