    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-5-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Compensation for acquisition of property",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-5-sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.42",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf the operation of this Schedule would result in an acquisition of\nproperty (within the meaning of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution)\nfrom a person otherwise than on just terms (within the meaning of that\nparagraph), the Commonwealth is liable to pay a reasonable amount of\ncompensation to the person.\n(2)\nIf the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount of the\ncompensation, the person may institute proceedings in a court of\ncompetent jurisdiction for the recovery from the Commonwealth of\nsuch reasonable amount of compensation as the court determines.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nMinor amendments  Schedule 6\n\nNo. 12, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nIf the operation of this Schedule would result in an acquisition of\nproperty (within the meaning of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution)\nfrom a person otherwise than on just terms (within the meaning of that\nparagraph), the Commonwealth is liable to pay a reasonable amount of\ncompensation to the person.\n(2)\nIf the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount of the\ncompensation, the person may institute proceedings in a court of\ncompetent jurisdiction for the recovery from the Commonwealth of\nsuch reasonable amount of compensation as the court determines.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nMinor amendments  Schedule 6\n\nNo. 12, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-5-sec-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-5-sec-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "40f7ff3c5204f691b3218f2f3ef66c7c5ce1a4b27a03558773f8480dcfd02aea",
      "skos:note": "Compensation for acquisition of property on just terms"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-5-sec-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 Compensation for acquisition of property",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 42,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf the operation of this Schedule would result in an acquisition of\nproperty (within the meaning of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution)\nfrom a person otherwise than on just terms (within the meaning of that\nparagraph), the Commonwealth is liable to pay a reasonable amount of\ncompensation to the person.\n(2)\nIf the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount of the\ncompensation, the person may institute proceedings in a court of\ncompetent jurisdiction for the recovery from the Commonwealth of\nsuch reasonable amount of compensation as the court determines.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012\n\nMinor amendments  Schedule 6\n\nNo. 12, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015"
    },
